The next day, I go to the FRRO office.
It is a big government office.
I have all my documents.
I go to the counter.
I speak to the official.
I say, "Hello, sir."
He says, "Hello, madam."
"Do you have your passport?"
I say, "Yes, sir, I have my passport and visa."
I give my documents to him.
He looks at the documents.
He asks, "What is your Indian phone number?"
I say, "I have a new number."
"It is nine eight seven six five, four three two one zero."
He writes the number in the computer.
He asks, "What is your age?"
I say, "I am thirty-one years old."
He says, "Your registration is complete."
I say, "Thank you, sir."
Now I have everything.
